{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013PSbskujK4h4fA5xTFFUBH","type":"tool_result","content":"The abstract doesn't include the Arrhenius equation, any numerical self-diffusion coefficients, or the activation energy values. It mentions the Arrhenius equation and the Murday comparison only in passing. Quotes are split into segments under 125 characters:\n\n> \"Little liquid lithium experimental self-diffusion coefficient were reported in the literature\"\n\n> \"In the paper, the EAM potential is applied to calculate self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium\"\n\n> \"with emphasis on a wide range of temperature, pressure, magnetic field, and gravity acceleration.\"\n\n> \"The results show that the liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient increases with temperature increasing\"\n\n> \"and decreases with pressure increasing.\"\n\n> \"Calculated self-diffusion coefficient is in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere.\"\n\n> \"We get the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results.\"\n\n> \"The increasing of pressure enlarges the liquid lithium activation energy\"\n\n> \"and lowers the movement of atom in liquid lithium.\"\n\nFor the actual Arrhenius fit and numerical values, you would need the full article at the DOI listed on the page (10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38c2b3be-e29f-40aa-8a94-71de4b72e65a","uuid":"d4ab386b-02b4-4ed4-b77d-5260b846a014","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:57:28.124Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":43947,"code":200,"codeText":"200","result":"The abstract doesn't include the Arrhenius equation, any numerical self-diffusion coefficients, or the activation energy values. It mentions the Arrhenius equation and the Murday comparison only in passing. Quotes are split into segments under 125 characters:\n\n> \"Little liquid lithium experimental self-diffusion coefficient were reported in the literature\"\n\n> \"In the paper, the EAM potential is app