{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QyVa4pndSEP3k7MLopbjNL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"liquid lithium\" self-diffusion \"Murday\" \"10^-5 cm^2/s\" OR \"×10−5 cm2/s\" ab initio molecular dynamics comparison experiment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ab initio Monte Carlo simulations for finite-temperature properties: Application to lithium clusters and bulk liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0208335\"},{\"title\":\"Suitability of ReaxFF potential for MD modelling of lithium across low and high temperatures\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.00807\"},{\"title\":\"independent.academia.edu\",\"url\":\"https://independent.academia.edu/DavidFarrell12\"},{\"title\":\"arch.neicon.ru\",\"url\":\"https://arch.neicon.ru/xmlui/handle/123456789/1928725\"},{\"title\":\"Calculations of atomic dynamics in simple liquid metals\",\"url\":\"https://acikerisim.trakya.edu.tr/items/26b3e66d-0537-4f4d-b725-259df065b525/full\"},{\"title\":\"investiga.upo.es\",\"url\":\"https://investiga.upo.es/documentos/5ec795a52999520a1d559bd6\"},{\"title\":\"https-meetings--archive-aps-org-443.webvpn1.xju.edu.cn\",\"url\":\"https://https-meetings--archive-aps-org-443.webvpn1.xju.edu.cn/mar/2018/v31/12/\"},{\"title\":\"Calculations of atomic dynamics in simple liquid metals\",\"url\":\"https://avesis.trakya.edu.tr/yayin/455a3393-00d0-4e5d-b406-b38d1a09215b/calculations-of-atomic-dynamics-in-simple-liquid-metals\"},{\"title\":\"Liquid li structure and dynamics: A comparison between OFDFT and second nearest-neighbor embedded-atom method\",\"url\":\"https://collaborate.princeton.edu/en/publications/liquid-li-structure-and-dynamics-a-comparison-between-ofdft-and-s/\"},{\"title\":\"investiga.upo.es\",\"url\":\"https://investiga.upo.es/documentos/5ec795a52999520a1d559bd6?lang=en\"}]\n\nI ran one search. It didn't find a source giving a liquid-lithium self-diffusion value of about 10^-5 cm²/s, so I can't confirm that figure. The closest match is a 2025 arXiv paper on ReaxFF potentials for lithium MD. It compares lithium diffusivities from several models against experimental data from Yakimovich and Murday. The diffusivities of pure Li obtained with 2NN-Meam potential, ReaxFF potential, and DFT-MD were compared with experimental results of Yakimovich and Murday. Its findings:\n\n- **DFT-MD:** The DFT results are somewhat underestimating the experiment over the whole range of liquid Li temperatures.\n- **ReaxFF:** it somewhat overestimates the experimental data at higher temperatures.\n- **Classical MEAM:** it falls exactly to the experimental data in the paper's comparison.\n- **Murday data:** The old experimental data of Murday underestimates all the calculated data.\n\nThe results don't give the absolute numbers, so check the paper's figure 4 for the actual values.\n\nOther results were less relevant. An ab initio Monte Carlo study compared liquid-lithium structure (pair correlation functions) with ab initio MD and X-ray data, not diffusion. Orbital-free ab initio molecular dynamics was applied to liquid lithium at 470 K and 725 K in a structure-factor comparison with scattering experiments. A 2011 paper compared orbital-free first-principles MD with classical MEAM for self-diffusion and other properties, but the search didn't show its numbers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38c2b3be-e29f-40aa-8a94-71de4b72e65a","uuid":"fd19f805-539d-452e-b99f-e285c6a4bca4","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:57:39.560Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"liquid lithium\" self-diffusion \"Murday\" \"10^-5 cm^2/s\" OR \"×10−5 cm2/s\" ab initio molecular dynamics comparison experiment","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LQpDjVJ7ovwJjFPn1K3RTH","content":[{"title":"Ab initio Monte Carlo simulations for finite-temperature properties: Application to lithium clusters and bulk liquid lithium