erestimates the experimental data at higher temperatures.\n- **Classical MEAM:** it falls exactly to the experimental data in the paper's comparison.\n- **Murday data:** The old experimental data of Murday underestimates all the calculated data.\n\nThe results don't give the absolute numbers, so check the paper's figure 4 for the actual values.\n\nOther results were less relevant. An ab initio Monte Carlo study compared liquid-lithium structure (pair correlation functions) with ab initio MD and X-ray data, not diffusion. Orbital-free ab initio molecular dynamics was applied to liquid lithium at 470 K and 725 K in a structure-factor comparison with scattering experiments. A 2011 paper compared orbital-free first-principles MD with classical MEAM for self-diffusion and other properties, but the search didn't show its numbers."],"durationSeconds":6.1592438519999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QyVa4pndSEP3k7MLopbjNL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
